#### 4. Fröbel / Napoleonic / Broodwich‑Method sequence

Ethical sequence (machine‑readable ordering):

```json
"curriculum_sequence": [
  "Froebel_Epistemic_Reconstruction",
  "Napoleonic_Governance_Epistemics",
  "Broodwich_Method_Kindergarten_Framework"
]
```

- **Fröbel first:** play, gardens, maternal care, anti‑authoritarian early childhood spaces.   [TSpace Repository](https://tspace.library.utoronto.ca/handle/1807/139078?mode=full)  [Springer](https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-981-15-7435-1_20.pdf)  
- **Napoleonic governance next:** centralized state schooling, discipline, bureaucratic epistemics.  
- **Broodwich‑Method last:** mythic/absurdist frame that asks “what happens when method becomes curse?”—used to interrogate *method as power*, not to entertain horror.

The gate enforces that darkness (Napoleonic control, Promised Neverland, Broodwich) is always bracketed by **play, sanctuary, and recovery**.

